  "articleBody": "Thinking about tiling right over your current floor? It's a common thought, but there are a few important things to think about first. You really need to check if that existing floor is up to the task. Is it completely flat, clean, and well-adhered? If not, you're setting yourself up for problems down the road, like cracked tiles or uneven surfaces. Often, it's safer and more effective to just remove the old flooring and start fresh with proper subfloor prep. This ensures a stable and long-lasting base for your new tiles. We often get asked about this, and our best advice is always to make sure the foundation is solid. If you're unsure about the condition of your subfloor or whether it can handle the weight and demands of new tile, it's definitely time to get a professional opinion. They can assess the situation and guide you on the best path forward to avoid costly mistakes.",
